stream - brings functional programming interface to you java code.
stream source - can be created from collections, lists, sets, ints, longs, doubles, 
stream operations - intermediate operation and terminal operation

intermediate operations - zero or more are allowed, order matters, filter first, then sort or map.
                        - for large datasets use parallel stream to enable multiple threads.
                        -anyMatch()
                        -distinct()
                        -filter()
                        -findFirst()
                        -flatMap()
                        -map()
                        -skip()
                        -sorted()

terminal operations - one termainal operation is allowed
                    - forEach applies same function to each element
                    - collect saves the elements into a collection
                    - other options reduce the stream into a single summary element -count() -max() -min() reduce() summmaryStatistics()


